# secrets — never commit real credentials. Ship .env.example only.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# logs — never commit runtime logs; they can carry unredacted PII (raw PANs/SSNs
# were found in a checked-in log; see docs/security-remediation-2026-07.md). If
# finance needs a sample, commit ONE redacted example explicitly. NOTE:
# untracking does not purge PII already in git history — a history rewrite
# (git filter-repo / BFG) is still required separately.
logs/
**/logs/
*.log

# secrets — never commit real credentials. The LLM/Bedrock key belongs in the
# host shell env or an untracked override file, NOT in the committed .env.
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# rag_eval harness artifacts (generated per run; report re-generated by python -m rag_eval.run)
rag_eval/.cache/
rag_eval/eval_report.md

# Claude Code config: track what a fresh clone needs, ignore personal/session state.
#
# EVERY skill under .claude/skills/ is tracked — the rule is a glob, not a list, so
# anything dropped there is shared with the team by that act alone. Keep a personal
# or experimental skill in ~/.claude/skills/ instead. (Do not re-add an enumeration
# of skill names here: the previous comment listed four and went stale the first time
# a fifth was added, claiming a narrower policy than the rule enforces.)
#
# `!.claude/skills/` re-includes the directory (its children then track fine today);
# `!.claude/skills/**` keeps nested skill files addable even if `.claude/*` is ever
# broadened to `.claude/**` (a recursive ignore would otherwise re-exclude them).
# `!.claude/settings.json` tracks the SHARED hook config so a clone inherits it.
# settings.local.json stays ignored — per-developer permission grants and plugin
# choices, which are personal and must not be forced on a clone.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/settings.json

# feature-status-tracker.md is a personal working log — candid review histories, brief
# corrections and defect post-mortems that must not reach the remote. The canonical copy
# moved outside the repo to
# ~/.claude/projects/-Users-maha-Desktop-revature-MC-meridian-lending/feature-status-tracker.md
# on 2026-08-13, and what stayed tracked here was a 7-line 3-row decoy of it whose rows
# said PR-Raised for weeks 2 and 3 long after #6 and #7 merged. Ignored so no branch can
# carry a decoy to origin again, and so the file cannot fork per branch (an untracked
# file has no per-branch identity). It is also what kept the tree chronically dirty,
# which made `make prove` abort.
#
# Ignoring it does NOT affect doc-path-lint: is_pathish() in scripts/check_doc_paths.sh
# requires a candidate to contain a slash, so a bare root-level filename was never
# graded as a path — see the comment at the head of that script.
#
# git overwrites an ignored file without warning on a branch switch. The canonical copy
# is outside the repo, so there is nothing here to lose; if you start keeping local rows
# in this path anyway, copy them out before switching branches.
feature-status-tracker.md
